666 0 obj
<< /ActualText (You'll see the word watt-hours a lot. It's how we measure daily power\nuse. If something uses 60 watts and runs for 10 hours, that's 600\nwatt-hours. Your fridge uses about 60W and runs all day, so roughly\n1,440 Wh per day.) /K [ 39 ] /P 665 0 R /Pg 7 0 R /S /Span /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
667 0 obj
<< /K [ 40 668 0 R ] /P 115 0 R /Pg 7 0 R /S /P /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
668 0 obj
<< /ActualText (That daily number drives everything. The battery size, the amount of\nsolar, the whole lot. Section 2 helps you work out yours. It takes\nabout 10 minutes.) /K [ 41 ] /P 667 0 R /Pg 7 0 R /S /Span /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
